                  "engine/review/fsstore/bypath.go:44-66",
                  "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go:24-33"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "R1-held-linux-root-follow",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go:96-100",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The root is opened following symlinks by design (documented as the caller-named working tree). Intermediate components of the path are opened with O_NOFOLLOW relative to held fds, so no escape from the results directory is reachable via the feature or name inputs. No exploitable issue found; the unsafe linkat syscall uses valid NUL-terminated pointers kept alive across the call.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go:96-100"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 9 changed paths in full.",
              "held_linux.go opens each path component with openat O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY relative to the parent fd, stages the temp file and links with linkat relative to the held fd, closing the baseline's check-then-use symlink race on linux; descriptor-leak test covers error paths.",
              "checkName and review.CheckFeature still gate name and feature before any filesystem access, so no traversal via inputs.",
              "bypath.go adds Lstat/SameFile re-verification before and after the link; behavior on valid baseline input is preserved, with Names now additionally hiding .review-*.tmp files and sorting on linux.",
              "No secrets, dependencies, or new external inputs were introduced."
