            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 9 changed paths for failure handling, cleanup, retry safety and descriptor leaks. No concrete production failure mode was found.",
              "In engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go, deferred cleanup runs in the right order: the temporary file is unlinked before the directory descriptor is closed. Every error path in openHeld and openBelow closes the descriptors it opened, and a descriptor-leak test covers the return paths.",
              "In the by-path store, a failed re-check returns before the link, and the staged file is discarded. A change detected after the link is reported with the file already linked, which is documented and tested.",
              "Names sorts the listing explicitly on Linux, so the baseline's sorted ReadDir order is preserved. Temporary files are filtered out of the listing on both implementations."
            ]
          }
        }
