            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R2-temp-name-duplicated",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go:176",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "stageAt hardcodes the temporary file name shape (\".review-\" + number + \".tmp\"), while Names hides temporary files through isTemporary, which matches against tempPattern. The two are tied only by a convention that nothing enforces. If tempPattern changes and this literal does not, Names would list in-flight temporary files as results, or hide real ones. A shared constant, or a test that builds the name from tempPattern, would remove the risk.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/review/fsstore/held_linux.go:176",
                  "engine/review/fsstore/fsstore.go:97"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 9 changed paths in the supplied patch. The held and by-path implementations are readable overall and their comments explain the intent.",
              "The Linux-held temp-name literal duplicates knowledge held in tempPattern, which the by-path implementation obtains from atomicfile via that pattern. The line number for held_linux.go is estimated from the patch, since the patch does not number its lines.",
              "namesByPath returns sorted names only because os.ReadDir sorts, while namesHeld sorts explicitly. This is a minor undocumented asymmetry and is not reported as a finding."
            ]
          }
